&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Sol-Floorwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/floor-trust/sol. Handback to
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/floor-trust/sol/out2.md (NOT final.md), under 1100 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. No git writes, no suites. Web allowed; cite URLs.
Code: /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine (span head, read only).

WAVE TWO (the ratchet). Common brief: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/floor-trust/brief-common.md. Your wave one: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/floor-trust/sol/own-wave1.md. Your peer's:
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/floor-trust/sol/peer-wave1.md. Read all three, then the code again where you split.

You agree: W14, W15, W16 share ONE shape (a signed floor statement bound to the place KEL head, filed by causal descent,
never first-wins); the place KEL authorizes the signer and the Nexus AID never signs as the place; a fork refuses or
surfaces, never picks by arrival; an offline reader holds its last accepted head and says "as of my last sync"; first
contact needs an anchor conveyed apart from the card (genesis, an authenticated admit, a person's deliberate transfer);
a cofounded partial carries the statement and files it only atomically with the quorum-counted carry; the herm carries
it opaque. Settle:

F1. THE NAME. Sol: "floor standing". Luna: "Floor Position". One name, one relation: grep the house for each word's
existing relations ("standing" already names realm standing, "standsInRealm", "a vessel standing"; "position"
already names causal position). Pick the name that collides with no held relation, or a third, and say why.
F2. THE RELEASE-HEAD AXIS. Luna binds the release head into the statement (two axes: key rotation and content update);
Sol lets it accompany as evidence and keeps the release record governing canon (W26 owns releases and the porch).
Read W26's floor release (docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem, floor-answer.ts, floor-porch.ts): does a gate pin's
ordering ever need the release head, or does binding it fuse two relations?
F3. A PIN CHANGE WITHOUT A KEY ROTATION. Sol wants a signed per-route successor event; does that case exist (measure:
what changes a floor gate pin besides a place key rotation? route keys, transport keys per (tier, Nexus, route) in
gate-bundle.ts)? If the pin derives from the place key, a KEL event alone orders it.
F4. THE PLACE KEL TODAY AND X0. Road :207 says the place signs under a pre-rotated KEL but code commits no next key, and
X0 carries the place KEL's pre-rotation. MEASURE the place KEL in code (sequence, event digest, rotation event,
next-key commitment). Can the floor statement bind (place AID, sequence, event digest) today? Does building this
lane need the pre-rotation built first (a build, not a bake), and should that build ride inside this lane (build
the end state) or its own lane before it? X0 bakes; it builds nothing.
F5. THE OPERATOR LIST. Sort every remaining question into: (a) canon already rules it (quote), (b) derivable from house
law (say which law), (c) truly the operator's, with options and one lean. Surface only (c).
F6. THE KIT, final: slices in order, files held, each red with its control and known positive, and the overlap
contract with W26 (release owner), W28 (gate files), K17-R (frontier verifier).

